<title>COLOMBIA: SOCCER-PERU BEAT COLOMBIA 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PERU BEAT COLOMBIA 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>BARRANQUILLA, Colombia 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru beat Colombia 1-0 (halftime 0-0) in a South American World Cup qualifier on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorer: Jose Pereda (61)</p>
<p>Attendance; 30,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Paraguay    10  7  2  1  15  6 23</p>
<p> Colombia    10  5  2  3  15  9 17</p>
<p> Argentina   10  4  4  2  14 10 16</p>
<p> Bolivia	9  3  4  2  14  9 13</p>
<p> Ecuador     10  4  1  5  14 12 13</p>
<p> Peru	  10  3  4  3  11 12 13</p>
<p> Uruguay     10  4  1  5  10 14 13</p>
<p> Chile	  9  3  3  3  17 12 12</p>
<p> Venezuela   10  0  1  9   6 32  1</p>
<p>Next matches: June 8 - Argentina v Peru, Ecuador v Chile, Uruguay v Colombia, Venezuela v Bolivia</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
